WEBVTT

00:00.590 --> 00:02.850
The continuous
function f is defined

00:02.850 --> 00:05.000
on the interval
negative 4 is less than

00:05.000 --> 00:07.870
or equal to x is less
than or equal to 3.

00:07.870 --> 00:11.480
The graph of f consists of two
quarter circles and one line

00:11.480 --> 00:12.330
segment.

00:12.330 --> 00:14.620
So this right here is
one quarter circle,

00:14.620 --> 00:16.350
then we have another
quarter circle,

00:16.350 --> 00:18.850
and then it has this
line segment over here,

00:18.850 --> 00:20.080
as shown in the figure above.

00:20.080 --> 00:21.746
I put the figure on
the side, so that we

00:21.746 --> 00:24.170
have some screen real
estate down here.

00:24.170 --> 00:28.450
Let g of x be equal to 2x plus
the definite integral from 0

00:28.450 --> 00:31.020
to x of f of t dt.

00:31.020 --> 00:33.320
All right, that's a
little bit interesting.

00:33.320 --> 00:34.970
Now, let's do Part a.

00:34.970 --> 00:35.690
Part a.

00:35.690 --> 00:38.030
Find g of negative 3.

00:38.030 --> 00:40.350
So we want to find
g of negative 3.

00:40.350 --> 00:42.680
So first of all, it
tells us what g of x is.

00:42.680 --> 00:45.239
So g of negative 3,
every time we see an x,

00:45.239 --> 00:46.530
we just put a negative 3 there.

00:46.530 --> 00:48.790
So it's going to
be 2 times negative

00:48.790 --> 00:56.610
3 plus the definite integral
from 0 to negative 3, f

00:56.610 --> 00:59.730
of t dt.

00:59.730 --> 01:01.930
So this first part is
pretty straightforward.

01:01.930 --> 01:05.604
2 times negative
3 is negative 6.

01:05.604 --> 01:07.020
And then this part
right over here

01:07.020 --> 01:10.335
is the definite integral from
0 to negative 3 of f of t dt.

01:16.010 --> 01:21.470
So this is essentially
the area under f of t--

01:21.470 --> 01:25.724
or under f of x, if you want to
view it that way-- from 0 to 3.

01:25.724 --> 01:27.140
And this is pretty
straightforward

01:27.140 --> 01:29.840
to figure out but we
have to be careful here.

01:29.840 --> 01:33.380
Because this area
right over here,

01:33.380 --> 01:35.750
this would be the integral--
let me do this in a color

01:35.750 --> 01:36.810
that you can see.

01:36.810 --> 01:38.720
That area right
over there would be

01:38.720 --> 01:45.590
the integral from
negative 3 to 0 f of t,

01:45.590 --> 01:50.460
or we could even say f of t
dt or f of x dx, either way.

01:50.460 --> 01:52.460
That would be this
area right over here.

01:52.460 --> 01:53.430
They've swapped it.

01:53.430 --> 01:55.750
They have the larger
number as the lower bound.

01:55.750 --> 01:57.920
They have 0 as the lower bound.

01:57.920 --> 02:00.090
So what we could do,
we could rewrite this.

02:00.090 --> 02:03.250
This is the same thing,
this is equal to negative 6

02:03.250 --> 02:06.880
minus-- if you swap the
bounds of integration,

02:06.880 --> 02:09.139
you swap the sign
on the integral.

02:09.139 --> 02:16.810
So we could say minus from
negative 3 to 0 of f of t dt.

02:16.810 --> 02:19.920
And now this thing right over
here-- this expression right

02:19.920 --> 02:25.485
over here is the area
under this quarter circle.

02:25.485 --> 02:27.110
And the area under
this quarter circle,

02:27.110 --> 02:29.670
we can just use a little bit
of geometry to figure that out.

02:29.670 --> 02:31.160
We know its radius.

02:31.160 --> 02:33.350
The radius here is 3.

02:33.350 --> 02:34.960
Radius is equal to 3.

02:34.960 --> 02:37.580
The entire circle
is pi r squared.

02:37.580 --> 02:39.780
So the entire circle--
the area if this

02:39.780 --> 02:45.960
was an entire circle right over
here-- that area would be pi r

02:45.960 --> 02:46.460
squared.

02:46.460 --> 02:48.280
So pi times 3 squared.

02:48.280 --> 02:49.680
So 9 pi.

02:49.680 --> 02:54.580
So it would be 9 pi, but this is
only 1/4 of the entire circle.

02:54.580 --> 02:56.290
So we want to divide it by 4.

02:56.290 --> 02:59.290
So this right over here we'll
evaluate to 9 pi over 4.

02:59.290 --> 03:03.450
So Part a, we get it's
equal to negative 6, that's

03:03.450 --> 03:11.630
that right over there,
minus 9 pi over 4.

03:11.630 --> 03:13.710
And that's at least the
first part of Part a.

03:13.710 --> 03:16.030
Then they say find g prime of x.

03:16.030 --> 03:19.430
So let's find g prime of x.

03:19.430 --> 03:22.380
We did the first part of
Part a right over there.

03:22.380 --> 03:25.842
Then we need to
find g prime of x.

03:25.842 --> 03:28.050
Well, it's just going to be
the derivative of g of x.

03:28.050 --> 03:31.439
The derivative of 2x
is just going to be 2.

03:31.439 --> 03:33.980
And then the derivative-- and
this is the fundamental theorem

03:33.980 --> 03:36.190
of calculus right over
here-- the derivative

03:36.190 --> 03:39.350
of the definite integral
from 0 to x of f of t dt,

03:39.350 --> 03:40.705
that's just going to be f of x.

03:43.800 --> 03:45.740
So that is g prime of x.

03:45.740 --> 03:48.260
We did this second
part right over there.

03:48.260 --> 03:50.840
That is g prime of x.

03:50.840 --> 03:53.580
And then we need to
evaluate it at negative 3.

03:53.580 --> 03:58.510
So g prime of
negative 3 is going

03:58.510 --> 04:02.510
to be equal to 2
plus f of negative 3,

04:02.510 --> 04:06.300
which is equal to 2 plus-- and
let's look at our-- let's see

04:06.300 --> 04:08.500
what f of negative 3 is.

04:08.500 --> 04:10.030
This is our function definition.

04:10.030 --> 04:14.120
When x is equal to negative
3, our function is at 0.

04:14.120 --> 04:16.329
So f of negative 3 is just 0.

04:16.329 --> 04:19.680
So it's just two plus
0, which is equal to 2.

04:19.680 --> 04:22.300
So g of negative
3 is equal to 2.

04:22.300 --> 04:24.295
And we're done with Part a.

04:24.295 --> 04:25.920
And the trickiest
part of this is just

04:25.920 --> 04:28.580
realizing the bounds
of integration.

04:28.580 --> 04:31.565
That you might be tempted to
say, oh, the integral between 0

04:31.565 --> 04:33.690
and negative 3, that's
just this area over here

04:33.690 --> 04:35.330
because we're going
between 0 and negative 3.

04:35.330 --> 04:37.060
But you've got to
realize that we actually

04:37.060 --> 04:39.310
have to swap them and make
them negative if you really

04:39.310 --> 04:41.780
want to consider this
area right over here.

04:41.780 --> 04:44.470
That this integral is going to
be the negative of this area.

04:44.470 --> 04:46.928
And that's what we did when we
went through this step right

04:46.928 --> 04:47.780
over there.
